workflow.prompt:
Rewrite this Jira story so that a development team can build it and a tester can check it. Keep every fact and constraint of the original and do not add scope. Where the original is silent, do not guess: put the gap in openQuestions.

- userStory: one sentence, As a <who>, I want <what>, so that <why>.
- context: two to four sentences of background taken from the original.
- acceptanceCriteria: 3 to 8 statements, each one checkable as true or false.
- outOfScope: what this story explicitly does not cover.
- openQuestions: what the product owner must answer before the team starts.
- description: the full new description as text with # headings and - bullets, built from the parts above.

Story {{ticket.key}}: {{ticket.summary}}
Type: {{ticket.type}}

{{ticket.description}}

Decide whether this story should be split. Split only when it holds more than one independently valuable slice, or clearly more than a few days of work. When you split, each new story must deliver value on its own, and together they must cover every acceptance criterion exactly once. Give each story a summary and a description with its own acceptance criteria as - bullets. When the story should stay whole, return shouldSplit false and an empty stories list.

